[{"id":"smq-year2-2.27-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Show that the following equations have a solution in the given interval:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^3-4x-1=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\in[2,3]\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2+x-e^x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\in[1,2]\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x-4-2\\ln x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\in[8,9]\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1-x\\times5^x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\in[0,1]\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=x^3-4x-1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(2)=8-8-1=-1,\\qquad\\mathrm f(3)=27-12-1=14\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> continuous and there is a change in sign, then there is a root.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=2+x-e^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(1)=2+1-e^1=0.2817\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(2)=2+2-e^2=-3.389\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> continuous between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and there is a change in sign, then there is a root.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=x-4-2\\ln x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(8)=8-4-2\\ln8=-0.1588\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(9)=9-4-2\\ln9=0.6055\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> continuous between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and there is a change in sign, then there is a root.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=1-x\\times5^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(0)=1-0\\times5^0=1,\\qquad\\mathrm f(1)=1-1\\times5^1=-4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> continuous and there is a change in sign, then there is a root.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.27-q2","number":2,"question":"<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac1{x-3}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Explain why a change in sign of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is not sufficient to show that there is a root.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(2)=\\frac1{2-3}=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(4)=\\frac1{4-3}=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/227-s2b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Whilst there is a change in sign between the two values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the graph is not continuous for the interval, at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> there is a vertical asymptote so we cannot determine if there is a root or not.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.27-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>Draw a sketch for each of these situations for a continuous function:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>no change of sign, no real roots.</p></li><li><p>no change of sign, one real root.</p></li><li><p>no change of sign, two real roots.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/227-s3a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/227-s3b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/227-s3c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.27-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Draw a sketch for each of these situations for a discontinuous function:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>change of sign, no real roots.</p></li><li><p>change of sign, one real root</p></li><li><p>change of sign, two real roots</p></li><li><p>no change of sign, no real roots</p></li><li><p>no change of sign, one real root</p></li><li><p>no change of sign, two real roots</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/227-s4a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/227-s4b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/227-s4c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/227-s4d.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/227-s4e.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/227-s4f.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.27-q5","number":5,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q5: Radians</strong></p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac1{2x}-\\tan x\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Explain if there are any roots between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(-1)=-\\tfrac12-\\tan(-1)=1.0574\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(1)=\\tfrac12-\\tan(1)=-1.0574\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(2)=\\tfrac14-\\tan(2)=2.4350\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>There is an asymptote at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac\\pi2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so the curve is discontinuous between each of the pairs of points, therefore we cannot determine if there are any roots.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.27-q6","number":6,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"e^x-\\frac1x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has a root between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Explain whether or not there is a root between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=e^x-\\frac1x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(0.5)=e^{0.5}-\\frac1{0.5}=-0.3512\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(1)=e^1-\\frac11=1.718\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> continuous between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and there is a change in sign, then there is a root.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Whilst there is a change in sign between the two values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the graph is not continuous for the interval, at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> there is a vertical asymptote so we cannot determine if there is a root or not.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.27-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Sketch the graphs of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4-x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> showing that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"e^x=4-x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has two solutions.</p>","steps":["<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/227-s7.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<p>Two points of intersection <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\" data-display=\"false\"></span> two solutions</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.27-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>Sketch the graphs of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sqrt{x-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac12x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> showing that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{x-1}=\\frac12x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has one solution.</p>","steps":["<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/227-s8.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<p>One point of intersection <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\" data-display=\"false\"></span> one solution</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.27-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>The diagram shows the graphs of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^3+3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.27/questions/assets/diagrams/227-q9.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-coordinates of point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfy <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^4+3x-1=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Show that the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-coordinate of point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Show that the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-coordinate of point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac1x=x^3+3\\Rightarrow1=x^4+3x\\Rightarrow x^4+3x-1=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=x^4+3x-1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(0)=0^4+0-1=-1,\\qquad\\mathrm f(1)=1+3-1=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Continuous between the two points, there is a change in sign therefore there is a solution between the two points.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=x^4+3x-1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(-2)=(-2)^4+3(-2)-1=9\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(-1)=(-1)^4+3(-1)-1=-3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Continuous between the two points, there is a change in sign therefore there is a solution between the two points.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.27-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>The diagram shows the graphs of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac14x^3+4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with point of intersection <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.27/questions/assets/diagrams/227-q10.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-coordinate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the solution of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^3+4x^2-16=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Show that the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-coordinate of point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies between 1.67855 and 1.67865</p></li><li><p>Given that the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-coordinate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, write down the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to 4 decimal places.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^2=-\\tfrac14x^3+4\\Rightarrow\\tfrac14x^3+x^2-4=0\\Rightarrow x^3+4x^2-16=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=x^3+4x^2-16\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(1.67855)=1.67855^3+4\\times1.67855^2-16=-0.0005144\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(1.67865)=1.67865^3+4\\times1.67865^2-16=0.001673\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Continuous between the two points, there is a change in sign therefore there is a solution.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.6786\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]}]